{"tool_name":"agreg-snpdb","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"agreg-snpdb","home":"https://azifi.tz.agrar.uni-goettingen.de/agreg-snpdb","summary":"A Database of Regulatory SNPs for Agricultural Animal Species.","addition_date":"2021-12-09T10:09:12.518564Z","last_update_date":"2021-12-09T10:09:12.521758Z","tool_type":["Database portal"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:agreg-snpdb","credit":[{"email":"gueltas.mehmet@fh-swf.de","name":"Mehmet G\u00fcltas","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3297-3192","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"selina.klees@uni-goettingen.de","name":"Selina Klees","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7640-6523","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Nucleic acids-binding site prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0420"},{"term":"Promoter prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0440"},{"term":"SNP annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3661"},{"term":"SNP detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0484"}]}],"name":"agReg-SNPdb","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.3390/BIOLOGY10080790","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021 by the authors. Licensee MDPI, Basel, Switzerland.Transcription factors (TFs) govern transcriptional gene regulation by specifically binding to short DNA motifs, known as transcription factor binding sites (TFBSs), in regulatory regions, such as promoters. Today, it is well known that single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) in TFBSs can dramatically affect the level of gene expression, since they can cause a change in the binding affinity of TFs. Such SNPs, referred to as regulatory SNPs (rSNPs), have gained attention in the life sciences due to their causality for specific traits or diseases. In this study, we present agReg-SNPdb, a database comprising rSNP data of seven agricultural and domestic animal species: cattle, pig, chicken, sheep, horse, goat, and dog. To identify the rSNPs, we constructed a bioinformatics pipeline and identified a total of 10,623,512 rSNPs, which are located within TFBSs and affect the binding affinity of putative TFs. Altogether, we implemented the first systematic analysis of SNPs in promoter regions and their impact on the binding affinity of TFs for livestock and made it usable via a web interface.","authors":[{"name":"Gultas M."},{"name":"Heinrich F."},{"name":"Klees S."},{"name":"Schmitt A.O."}],"date":"2021-08-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Biology","title":"Agreg-snpdb: A database of regulatory snps for agricultural animal species"},"pmcid":"PMC8389679","pmid":"34440019"}],"topic":[{"term":"Agricultural science","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3810"},{"term":"DNA polymorphism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2885"},{"term":"Gene regulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0204"},{"term":"Transcription factors and regulatory sites","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0749"},{"term":"Zoology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3500"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"agReg-SNPdb","home":"https://bio.tools/agreg-snpdb","summary":"A Database of Regulatory SNPs for Agricultural Animal Species.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:agreg-snpdb/db/azifi.tz.agrar.uni-goettingen.de","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":5,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2023"},{"count":1,"year":"2024"},{"count":3,"year":"2022"}],"doi":"10.3390/biology10080790","pmcid":"PMC8389679","pmid":"34440019","ref_count":53,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1988"},{"count":1,"year":"1996"},{"count":1,"year":"1997"},{"count":1,"year":"1998"},{"count":1,"year":"2004"},{"count":1,"year":"2009"},{"count":1,"year":"2017"},{"count":2,"year":"2003"},{"count":2